{"name":"Quarterdeck","hex":"#1272a3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quarterdeck","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The aft part of the upper deck of a ship; normally reserved for officers"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarterdeck"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quarterdeck","blocks":[{"text":"The quarterdeck is a raised deck behind the main mast of a sailing ship. Traditionally it was where the captain commanded his vessel and where the ship's colours were kept. This led to its use as the main ceremonial and reception area on board, and the word is still used to refer to such an area on a ship or even in naval establishments on land. Many such facilities have areas decorated like shipboard quarterdecks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Quarter_Deck_Frigate.jpg/330px-Quarter_Deck_Frigate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quarterdeck","wikidata":"Q10516659"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/HMS_Londonderry_%28F_108%29_off_Miami_1964.jpg/500px-HMS_Londonderry_%28F_108%29_off_Miami_1964.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/HMS_Londonderry_%28F_108%29_off_Miami_1964.jpg/1280px-HMS_Londonderry_%28F_108%29_off_Miami_1964.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/HMS_Londonderry_%28F_108%29_off_Miami_1964.jpg/500px-HMS_Londonderry_%28F_108%29_off_Miami_1964.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Before helicopter decks became common, warships such as the Rothesay class often had a deck at the stern used for secondary armament.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHMS_Londonderry_(F_108)_off_Miami_1964.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/USS_Colorado_%28BB-45%29_New_York_1932.jpg/500px-USS_Colorado_%28BB-45%29_New_York_1932.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/USS_Colorado_%28BB-45%29_New_York_1932.jpg/1280px-USS_Colorado_%28BB-45%29_New_York_1932.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/USS_Colorado_%28BB-45%29_New_York_1932.jpg/500px-USS_Colorado_%28BB-45%29_New_York_1932.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Seaplanes were often operated from the quarterdeck of battleships, as here on USS Colorado","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSS_Colorado_(BB-45)_New_York_1932.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/QuarterdeckKatori.jpg/500px-QuarterdeckKatori.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/QuarterdeckKatori.jpg/500px-QuarterdeckKatori.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Quarterdeck of a Japanese warship. Note the watchstanders in uniform, the wooden plaque, and the proximity to the accommodation ladder.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuarterdeckKatori.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}